  "question": {
    "text": "In which of the following conversions, phosphorus pentachloride is used as the reagent?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WcZZ9",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z86MR",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WT87l",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{Cl}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BYiB2",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CHCl}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When ethyl alcohol is treated with $\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}$, then ethyl chloride is formed.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{OH} &+\\mathrm{PCl}_{5} \\longrightarrow_{\\Delta} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{HCl}+\\mathrm{POCl}_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
